<section class="section wrap role-fit" id="role-fit">
 <div class="section-head"><div><p class="label">3 / EXPERIENCE &amp; ROLE FIT</p><h2>The experience I bring.<br/>How it fits the role.</h2></div><p>My experience connects AI governance, workflow analysis and model evaluation. Here is how I would bring that foundation to the Strategic Projects Associate, Safety role.</p></div>
 <div class="fit-stats" aria-label="Selected experience, rounded for confidentiality">
  <div><strong>2k+</strong><span>automation cases analyzed</span></div><div><strong>800+</strong><span>approval requests reviewed</span></div><div><strong>10+</strong><span>model candidates compared</span></div><div><strong>3</strong><span>survey languages supported</span></div>
 </div>
 <p class="small">Selected figures from separate projects; counts are rounded and do not represent safety annotation volumes. Role mapping uses the supplied Handshake job description, reviewed October 19, 2026.</p>
 <div class="responsibility-heading"><div><span class="label">BROWSE MY ROLE RESPONSIBILITIES</span><h3>My role, from brief to delivery.</h3></div><p>Follow the work pipeline. Click any task to see what I would do and the experience I bring.</p></div>
 <div class="responsibility-map">{workGroups.map(([title,flow],group)=><section class="responsibility-stage"><header><span>0{group+1}</span><h4>{title}</h4><p>{flow}</p></header><div>{responsibilities.map((work,i)=>work.group===group&&<button class="responsibility-trigger" type="button" data-work-open={i} aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls={`work-dialog-${i}`}><span class="work-icon" aria-hidden="true">{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><span><strong>{work.title}</strong><small>Open experience ↗</small></span><span class="work-plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>)}</div><p class="stage-deliverable"><span>STAGE OUTPUT</span>{['Scoped program + evaluation plan','Prepared reviewers + usable guidance','Quality findings + policy feedback','Delivery decisions + next actions'][group]}</p></section>)}</div>
 <p class="small">Mapped from the supplied job description. This pipeline is my interpretation of the work; tasks can overlap and repeat.</p>
 {responsibilities.map((work,i)=><dialog class="work-dialog" id={`work-dialog-${i}`} aria-labelledby={`work-title-${i}`}><div class="work-dialog-top"><span class="label">THE ROLE × MY EXPERIENCE · {i+1} / {responsibilities.length}</span><button type="button" data-work-close aria-label="Close experience">×</button></div><h3 id={`work-title-${i}`}>{work.title}</h3><p class="work-partners"><span>WORK WITH</span>{work.partners}</p><div class="work-dialog-grid"><section class="work-do"><span class="label">AT HANDSHAKE / MY APPROACH</span><ol>{work.steps.map(step=><li>{step}</li>)}</ol><div class="work-result"><span>OUTPUT</span><p>{work.deliverable}</p></div></section><section class="work-proof"><span class="label">MY RELATED EXPERIENCE</span><h4>{matches[work.match].title}</h4><p>{matches[work.match].evidence}</p><div class="work-result"><span>WHAT I PRODUCED</span><p>{matches[work.match].output}</p></div></section></div><div class="work-transfer"><span class="label">HOW THE EXPERIENCE TRANSFERS</span><p>{matches[work.match].apply}</p></div><p class="work-boundary">{matches[work.match].scope}</p><details class="work-jd"><summary>Responsibility in the job description</summary><p>{work.jd}</p></details><footer><button type="button" data-work-switch={(i+responsibilities.length-1)%responsibilities.length}>← Previous responsibility</button><button type="button" data-work-switch={(i+1)%responsibilities.length}>Next responsibility →</button></footer></dialog>)}
 <details class="fit-summary" id="presentation"><summary>How these experiences connect</summary><div class="fit-pitch"><h3>“My strength is connecting policy, data and execution.”</h3><p>In enterprise AI governance, I have worked on the practical questions behind adoption: what information a reviewer needs, where decisions become ambiguous, and how to make guidance useful. I analyzed more than 800 approval requests and delivered interactive reports that made classification gaps and unresolved workflow issues visible.</p><p>I also processed more than 2,000 multilingual automation cases in Python, refined categories and built dashboards with clear units of analysis. In human–AI research, I contributed to evaluation work involving more than 10 model candidates and 30 experimental conditions, investigating whether inconsistent behavior came from prompts, information states or the rules themselves.</p><p>That is the foundation I would bring to Handshake: clear review workflows, careful analysis and decision-ready communication. I would apply it to policy rubrics, reviewer calibration and quality reporting. My direct experience is in enterprise governance and research; I would learn the project’s safety policies and sensitive-content procedures before taking on independent judgments. I want to help teams understand why decisions differ, improve the guidance and measure whether the next batch is better.</p></div></details>
 <div class="section-head fit-plan-head"><div><p class="label">PROPOSED CONTRIBUTION</p><h3>My first 30 days: learn, pilot, improve.</h3></div><p>A discussion proposal, subject to the team’s priorities and authorized procedures.</p></div>
 <ol class="fit-plan"><li><span>DAYS 01–10</span><h4>Understand the decision</h4><p>Confirm policy owners, rubric versions, customer acceptance criteria and reviewer support procedures.</p><b>Output: workflow map + open-question log</b></li><li><span>DAYS 11–20</span><h4>Pilot and calibrate</h4><p>Review a scoped sample with authorized reviewers; document disagreement causes and escalate unresolved boundaries.</p><b>Output: pilot findings + revised examples</b></li><li><span>DAYS 21–30</span><h4>Track and improve</h4><p>Report quality by category alongside throughput, rework and turnaround. Agree on owners for the next improvement cycle.</p><b>Output: quality dashboard + action plan</b></li></ol>
 <details class="fit-development"><summary>Where I would build further experience</summary><p>Production safety annotation, high-severity harm review, formal inter-rater calibration, and frontier-lab delivery economics are areas where I would need project-specific training and supervised practice. I would confirm escalation routes, reviewer wellbeing support and access controls before handling sensitive material. I am not presenting the synthetic exercises below as past client work or achieved quality results.</p></details>
</section>

<script>
 let workOpener: HTMLElement | null = null;
 function openWork(id: string, opener?: HTMLElement) {
  const target=document.getElementById(`work-dialog-${id}`);
  if (!(target instanceof HTMLDialogElement)) return;
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLDialogElement>('.work-dialog[open]').forEach(dialog=>dialog.close());
  if(opener) workOpener=opener;
  target.showModal();
  document.body.classList.add('work-dialog-open');
 }
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-work-open]').forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',()=>openWork(button.dataset.workOpen!,button)));
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLDialogElement>('.work-dialog').forEach(dialog=>{
  dialog.querySelector('[data-work-close]')?.addEventListener('click',()=>dialog.close());
  dialog.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-work-switch]').forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',()=>openWork(button.dataset.workSwitch!)));
  dialog.addEventListener('click',event=>{if(event.target===dialog){const r=dialog.getBoundingClientRect();if(event.clientX<r.left||event.clientX>r.right||event.clientY<r.top||event.clientY>r.bottom)dialog.close();}});
  dialog.addEventListener('close',()=>{if(!document.querySelector('.work-dialog[open]')){document.body.classList.remove('work-dialog-open');workOpener?.focus({preventScroll:true});}});
 });
</script>
